<｜hy_begin_of_sentence:opensource｜># Tools

You may call one or more functions to assist with the user query.

You are provided with function signatures within <tools></tools> XML tags:
<tools>
{"function": {"description": "The weather in a city", "name": "get_weather", "parameters": {"properties": {"city": {"description": "La città", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["city"], "type": "object"}}, "type": "function"}
</tools>

For function call returns, you should first print <tool_calls:opensource>
For each function call, you should return object like:
<tool_call:opensource>{function-name}<tool_sep:opensource>
<arg_key:opensource>{arg-key-1}</arg_key:opensource>
<arg_value:opensource>{arg-value-1}</arg_value:opensource>
<arg_key:opensource>{arg-key-2}</arg_key:opensource>
<arg_value:opensource>{arg-value-2}</arg_value:opensource>
...
</tool_call:opensource>
At the end of function call returns, you should print </tool_calls:opensource><｜reasoning_mode:opensource｜>reasoning_effort:no_think<｜hy_User:opensource｜>What is the capital of France?<｜hy_Assistant:opensource｜><think:opensource></think:opensource>Paris.<｜hy_eos:opensource｜><｜hy_User:opensource｜>And of Italy?<｜hy_Assistant:opensource｜><think:opensource></think:opensource>